A||||9||GodSend||Steering Wheel Button. and other NOS particulars||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||11-28-2001||03:38 PM||||<P>I am dreaming of a nice NOS install next spring and I invision a nice little red push button on the steering wheel (or maybe the top of the shifter).  Has anyone done this, any ideas?<P>I have been reading up on "wet" versus "dry" systems.  I will be installing this kit myself, and am looking for a 50-60hp shot max (2.8 w/ 70,000 miles).  I know I can install a dry system for sure (sounds easy, I have done enough stereo installs in my time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) , but I have yet to find out exactly how difficult a "wet" system is to install? <P>(perhaps another silly question is, do a wet and dry use the same nos?).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||11-28-2001||03:55 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Interior_1a_1.jpg"> <BR>Not running NOS but both buttons on steering wheel are wired. Wheel made by grant, haven't seen it anywhere lately, this one was purchased from Summit.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||11-28-2001||04:49 PM||||I think NOS is best activated by a microswitch mounted under the throttle pedal or by the TPS.  That way you won't accidently trigger it at less than full throttle, which could lead to some pretty bad things happening.  Forget about the Fast and Furious.. that steering wheel button stuff was just for 'dramatic effect'<P>Yes, wet and dry use the same thing, N<sub>2</sub>0.  NOS is a brand name   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for the difficulties.. I dunno, never installed either.  Wet system is a litter safer (less chance of running lean) and you can get more power out of it, from what I've heard.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">           <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||11-28-2001||07:26 PM||||Very good point about the wheel "Standard", didn't think that one through all the way. I have hit the horn buttons accidently a few times!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||LT1 Chop Top||11-28-2001||07:51 PM||||My wheel (from the fantasitc Ausfiero) has an acccessary button, in addition to the central horn button.  I wired the horn to the accessary just to be 'cheekey'....well that and I really don't need Nos.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel3_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||11-29-2001||01:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>My wheel (from the fantasitc Ausfiero) has an acccessary button, in addition to the central horn button.  I wired the horn to the accessary just to be 'cheekey'....well that and I really don't need Nos.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Didn't use the accessory button???  Why don't you use that to activate the vibrating passenger seat?  There are a lot of chicks that would dig the power that car has, why not give them a <B>GREAT</B> ride <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Just make sure you use good seat covers..lol<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
